# UI label title case

Multi-word **field labels** and **section headers** must use title case (capitalize the first letter of each word).

Do **not** use `uppercase`, `tracking-wide`, or ALL CAPS styling for these labels.

## Scope

Apply to:
- Form field captions (`<label>`, `OutlinedTextField` labels, `legend`, etc.)
- Section group headings above controls (Templates, Flow, Muscle group, Log prompts, …)

Do **not** apply to:
- Dynamic content (exercise names, routine names, user-entered text)
- Button text, dialog titles, page titles, nav labels, toasts
- Single-word labels (already correct as-is)

## Web (`apps/web/web`)

Use the shared helpers — never raw text for multi-word labels:

```tsx
import { FieldLabel, SectionHeader } from "../components/FieldLabel";

<label className="label" htmlFor="name">
  <FieldLabel>Workout name</FieldLabel>
</label>

<SectionHeader>Rest between sets</SectionHeader>
```

Source text may stay lowercase in code; `FieldLabel` / `SectionHeader` call `titleCaseWords()`.

## Android (`app`)

Use the shared composables — never raw `Text("multi word …")` for field/section captions:

```kotlin
import com.erv.app.ui.components.FieldLabel
import com.erv.app.ui.components.FormSectionLabel
import com.erv.app.ui.components.FormSectionLabelMedium

// OutlinedTextField / text input
label = { FieldLabel("Rest between sets (seconds)") }

// Section above a control group
FormSectionLabel("Muscle group")
FormSectionLabelMedium("Log prompts")
```

For dynamic label strings, use `Text(label)` without title-casing.
